01:16:54,020 --> 01:16:55,610
Bedford Falls time...

1391
01:16:55,690 --> 01:16:57,980
Hey, Ernie. Look at that.

1392
01:17:03,490 --> 01:17:04,490
It's gonna snow again.

1393
01:17:04,570 --> 01:17:07,870
Look at the headlines. The President...

1394
01:17:07,950 --> 01:17:10,410
That's marvelous.

1395
01:17:10,500 --> 01:17:12,000
Commander Harry Bailey!

1396
01:17:12,080 --> 01:17:14,620
the second page.

1397
01:17:14,710 --> 01:17:15,960
Now, look, this is for you.

1398
01:17:16,040 --> 01:17:17,460
-Okay.

1399
01:17:17,540 --> 01:17:19,380
-See you again.

1400
01:17:21,050 --> 01:17:23,170
Be sure you spell the name right.

1401
01:17:34,310 --> 01:17:35,810
Extra! Read all about it!

1402
01:17:35,900 --> 01:17:38,360
on long-distance from Washington.

1403
01:17:38,440 --> 01:17:39,980
Harry! What do you know about that!

1404
01:17:40,070 --> 01:17:41,570
It's okay, isn't it?

1405
01:17:41,650 --> 01:17:43,940
Of course it is for a hero.

1406
01:17:44,030 --> 01:17:45,400
Harry!

1407
01:17:45,530 --> 01:17:49,580
a son of a gun. Congratulations.

1408
01:17:49,740 --> 01:17:52,240
How's Mother standing it? She did?

1409
01:17:52,580 --> 01:17:53,830
What do you know?

1410
01:17:53,910 --> 01:17:55,620
with the President's wife.

1411
01:17:55,710 --> 01:17:56,790
Wait till Martha hears about this.

1412
01:17:56,880 --> 01:17:59,000
-What'd they have to eat?

1413
01:17:59,090 --> 01:18:00,130
Harry,

1414
01:18:00,210 --> 01:18:03,340
in the town for you.

1415
01:18:03,420 --> 01:18:04,510
Oh, they are?

1416
01:18:04,590 --> 01:18:06,470
this afternoon.

1417
01:18:06,550 --> 01:18:07,680
In a plane?

1418
01:18:08,050 --> 01:18:10,180
What? Uncle Billy?

1419
01:18:10,260 --> 01:18:12,640
-He stopped at the bank first.

1420
01:18:12,720 --> 01:18:16,190
But look, now, tell me about it.

1421
01:18:16,270 --> 01:18:17,310
-What?

1422
01:18:17,400 --> 01:18:18,520
-What man?

1423
01:18:18,610 --> 01:18:20,190
Bank examiner.

1424
01:18:21,270 --> 01:18:23,400
will you?

1425
01:18:23,490 --> 01:18:24,690
I'll be right back.

1426
01:18:24,780 --> 01:18:26,240
-Harry.

1427
01:18:26,320 --> 01:18:28,820
-Carter, bank examiner.

1428
01:18:28,910 --> 01:18:31,030
-Merry Christmas.

1429
01:18:31,120 --> 01:18:32,870
We're all excited around here.

1430
01:18:32,950 --> 01:18:35,040
the Congressional Medal of Honor.

1431
01:18:35,120 --> 01:18:37,870
-Well, I guess they do those things.

1432
01:18:37,960 --> 01:18:40,790
-Good year?

1433
01:18:41,000 --> 01:18:44,130
Mr. Carter, we're broke.

1434
01:18:44,340 --> 01:18:46,010
Yeah, very funny.

1435
01:18:48,180 --> 01:18:50,970
come right in here, Mr. Carter.

1436
01:18:51,050 --> 01:18:53,310
when you okay reverse charges

1437
01:18:53,390 --> 01:18:55,140
on personal long-distance calls.

1438
01:18:55,230 --> 01:18:56,810
-No, no.

1439
01:18:56,890 --> 01:18:58,560
You just hold on, there.

1440
01:18:58,650 --> 01:19:01,400
I'd like to finish with you by tonight.

1441
01:19:01,480 --> 01:19:04,360
in Elmira with my family.

1442
01:19:04,440 --> 01:19:05,690
I don't blame you at all, Mr. Carter.

1443
01:19:05,780 --> 01:19:07,070
Just step right in here. We'll fix you up.

1444
01:19:08,110 --> 01:19:11,160
December 24.

1445
01:19:16,750 --> 01:19:19,330
$8,000.

1446
01:19:20,460 --> 01:19:23,040
-Merry Christmas.

1447
01:19:23,130 --> 01:19:26,550
What's the news?

1448
01:19:26,630 --> 01:19:30,380
wins Congressional Medal."

1449
01:19:30,470 --> 01:19:32,550
That couldn't be one of the Bailey boys.

1450
01:19:32,640 --> 01:19:36,220
now can you, Mr. Potter?

1451
01:19:36,310 --> 01:19:38,730
feel about that?

1452
01:19:38,810 --> 01:19:40,060
Very jealous. Very jealous.

1453
01:19:40,150 --> 01:19:42,350
He only lost three buttons off his vest.

1454
01:19:42,440 --> 01:19:44,480
slacker George would've gotten

1455
01:19:44,570 --> 01:19:46,440
two of these medals if he had gone.

1456
01:19:46,530 --> 01:19:48,070
-Yes.

1457
01:19:48,240 --> 01:19:51,700
like George had to stay at home.

1458
01:19:51,780 --> 01:19:55,830
in Germany and Japan.

1459
01:20:03,130 --> 01:20:06,840
-Good morning, Horace.

1460
01:20:07,880 --> 01:20:10,630
-Huh?

1461
01:20:10,720 --> 01:20:12,550
-What?

1462
01:20:12,640 --> 01:20:14,140
to make a deposit?

1463
01:20:14,220 --> 01:20:15,220
Oh, sure, sure I am.

1464
01:20:15,310 --> 01:20:18,720
to bring the money with you.

1465
01:20:19,270 --> 01:20:23,480
Oh, shucks, I knew I had.

1466
01:20:25,320 --> 01:20:27,400
How about that finger there?

1467
01:20:27,480 --> 01:20:28,570
Well, I...

1468
01:20:29,440 --> 01:20:30,650
Bailey.

1469
01:20:37,160 --> 01:20:39,580
Take me back there. Hurry up.

1470
01:20:41,670 --> 01:20:43,920
Come on, look sharp.

1471
01:21:01,600 --> 01:21:03,100
Take me back.

1472
01:21:12,950 --> 01:21:16,280
I got those books for you here.

1473
01:21:16,370 --> 01:21:17,780
Oh, hello, Vi.

1474
01:21:17,870 --> 01:21:19,450
George, can I see you for a second?

1475
01:21:19,540 --> 01:21:22,410
Go on in the office there.

1476
01:21:22,580 --> 01:21:25,420
He's on the telephone.

1477
01:21:26,210 --> 01:21:29,000
Long distance, Washington.

1478
01:21:29,090 --> 01:21:30,210
Hey, here's Harry on the phone.

1479
01:21:30,300 --> 01:21:32,050
remember? Harry.

1480
01:21:32,130 --> 01:21:33,380
-Hurry up.

1481
01:21:33,880 --> 01:21:37,640
Yes, Harry, yes, everything's fine.

1482
01:21:38,140 --> 01:21:40,350
I ought to have my head examined.

1483
01:21:40,430 --> 01:21:43,310
$8,000. It's got to be somewhere.

1484
01:21:49,480 --> 01:21:50,730
Here you are.

1485
01:21:51,320 --> 01:21:52,400
Character?

1486
01:21:53,030 --> 01:21:54,320
If I had any character, I'd...

1487
01:21:54,400 --> 01:21:57,820
your hometown and start all over again.

1488
01:21:57,910 --> 01:21:59,410
No, George, don't.

1489
01:21:59,490 --> 01:22:01,490
Here now, you're broke, aren't you?

1490
01:22:01,580 --> 01:22:03,200
-What do you want to do,

1491
01:22:03,290 --> 01:22:05,080
hock your furs and that hat?

1492
01:22:06,460 --> 01:22:07,920
You want to walk to New York?

1493
01:22:08,000 --> 01:22:09,790
for meals and rent up there,

1494
01:22:09,880 --> 01:22:11,300
in Bedford Falls.

1495
01:22:11,380 --> 01:22:13,170
-No, that's a loan, now.

1496
01:22:13,470 --> 01:22:15,760
That's my business, Building and Loan.

1497
01:22:15,930 --> 01:22:18,970
Good luck to you.

1498
01:22:19,050 --> 01:22:21,220
I'm glad I know you, George Bailey.

1499
01:22:26,440 --> 01:22:29,190
-Yeah, yeah, sure, I will.

1500
01:22:29,270 --> 01:22:31,190
once in a while.

1501
01:22:35,150 --> 01:22:38,450
-Merry Christmas, George.

1502
01:22:39,370 --> 01:22:41,830
-Oh, Mr. Carter, I'm sorry.

1503
01:22:41,910 --> 01:22:43,410
Uncle Billy in there?

1504
01:22:43,500 --> 01:22:45,000
Yeah, he's in his office.

1505
01:22:45,080 --> 01:22:47,290
What's going on?

1506
01:22:47,500 --> 01:22:49,500
The bank examiner's here.

1507
01:22:50,290 --> 01:22:53,210
-Yeah. He wants the accounts payable...

1508
01:22:53,340 --> 01:22:54,920
What's the matter with you?

1509
01:22:55,010 --> 01:22:56,420
Come here.

1510
01:23:16,700 --> 01:23:17,650
Eustace.

1511
01:23:17,740 --> 01:23:19,490
-Come here a minute.

1512
01:23:21,240 --> 01:23:23,490
with any cash last night?

1513
01:23:23,580 --> 01:23:26,080
before he closed up.

1514
01:23:27,250 --> 01:23:28,830
Now, look, did you buy anything?

1515
01:23:28,920 --> 01:23:31,210
-All right, all right.

1516
01:23:31,290 --> 01:23:33,920
since you left the house.

1517
01:23:34,000 --> 01:23:35,000
-Come on.

1518
01:23:44,930 --> 01:23:46,930
in your pocket?

1519
01:23:47,020 --> 01:23:50,140
Yeah, maybe, maybe.

1520
01:23:50,230 --> 01:23:53,020
We've got to find that money!

1521
01:23:53,110 --> 01:23:54,650
-Uncle Billy, look,

1522
01:23:54,730 --> 01:23:57,320
to happen if we don't find it?

1523
01:23:57,400 --> 01:23:58,440
Listen to me.

1524
01:23:58,530 --> 01:24:00,320
here in the house?

1525
01:24:00,410 --> 01:24:02,450
Someplace you hide the money?

1526
01:24:02,530 --> 01:24:04,160
I've gone over the whole house,

1527
01:24:04,240 --> 01:24:08,160
since I lost Laura.

1528
01:24:08,250 --> 01:24:11,370
Listen to me, listen to me! Think, think!

1529
01:24:11,460 --> 01:24:15,540
I can't think anymore. It hurts.

1530
01:24:15,630 --> 01:24:18,550
you silly, stupid old fool?

1531
01:24:18,630 --> 01:24:21,380
Do you realize what this means?

1532
01:24:21,470 --> 01:24:24,470
and prison!

1533
01:24:25,600 --> 01:24:26,890
That's what it means.

1534
01:24:26,970 --> 01:24:30,230
Well, it's not going to be me.

1535
01:24:53,000 --> 01:24:54,080
Hello, darling.

1536
01:24:54,170 --> 01:24:55,960
-Hello, Daddy.

1537
01:24:56,040 --> 01:24:57,920
How do you like it?

1538
01:24:58,000 --> 01:24:59,670
-Bless you!

1539
01:25:01,420 --> 01:25:02,590
Did you bring the wreath?

1540
01:25:02,680 --> 01:25:04,510
the Christmas wreath?

1541
01:25:04,590 --> 01:25:05,590
What wreath?

1542
01:25:05,680 --> 01:25:08,140
for the window.

1543
01:25:08,220 --> 01:25:09,560
No. I left it at the office.

1544
01:25:09,640 --> 01:25:11,600
-Yeah, it just started.

1545
01:25:11,680 --> 01:25:14,770
-Left them at the office.

1546
01:25:14,940 --> 01:25:16,020
What's the matter?

1547
01:25:16,110 --> 01:25:18,690
Everything's all right.

1548
01:25:26,370 --> 01:25:29,660
You can help me get this star up.

1549
01:25:29,740 --> 01:25:32,750
Way up at the top. There. That's it.

1550
01:25:33,370 --> 01:25:37,170
right there. Right there.

1551
01:25:39,380 --> 01:25:42,880
We're famous, George.

1552
01:25:42,970 --> 01:25:46,720
about the parade, the banquet.

1553
01:25:46,890 --> 01:25:48,970
Your mother's so excited. She...

1554
01:26:09,580 --> 01:26:12,080
Must she keep playing that?

1555
01:26:12,160 --> 01:26:15,000
for the party tonight, Daddy.

1556
01:26:15,080 --> 01:26:18,170
till midnight and sing Christmas carols.

1557
01:26:18,250 --> 01:26:19,750
Can you sing, Daddy?

1558
01:26:20,130 --> 01:26:21,710
Better hurry and shave.

1559
01:26:21,800 --> 01:26:24,760
-Families.

1560
01:26:24,840 --> 01:26:27,300
I don't want the families over here.

1561
01:26:29,100 --> 01:26:32,140
while I finish dinner.

1562
01:26:32,220 --> 01:26:35,310
Excuse me. Excuse me.

1563
01:26:35,440 --> 01:26:37,560
-Oh, yeah.

1564
01:26:37,650 --> 01:26:40,560
for the Baileys.

1565
01:26:41,020 --> 01:26:43,860
have a new car. You should see it.

1566
01:26:43,940 --> 01:26:46,200
Isn't it good enough for you?

1567
01:26:46,280 --> 01:26:47,360
Yes, Daddy.

1568
01:26:47,610 --> 01:26:50,030
Excuse me. Excuse me.

1569
01:26:50,120 --> 01:26:52,370
-I burped.

1570
01:26:53,450 --> 01:26:54,870
All right, darling, you're excused.

1571
01:26:54,950 --> 01:26:57,710
and see if little Zuzu wants anything.

1572
01:26:58,250 --> 01:27:02,540
-Oh, she's just got a cold. She's in bed.

1573
01:27:02,630 --> 01:27:04,090
Caught it coming home from school.

1574
01:27:04,170 --> 01:27:06,720
and she didn't want to crush it,

1575
01:27:06,800 --> 01:27:08,050
so she didn't button up her coat.

1576
01:27:08,130 --> 01:27:10,300
-It's just a cold.

1577
01:27:10,390 --> 01:27:11,680
-The doctor?

1578
01:27:11,760 --> 01:27:13,510
-Yes, I called him right away.

1579
01:27:13,600 --> 01:27:14,850
He says it's nothing to worry about.

1580
01:27:14,930 --> 01:27:16,230
What is it?

1581
01:27:16,310 --> 01:27:18,390
She'll be all right.

1582
01:27:18,480 --> 01:27:19,940
Of course, it's this old house.

1583
01:27:20,020 --> 01:27:22,230
we don't all have pneumonia.

1584
01:27:22,320 --> 01:27:26,650
Might as well be living in a refrigerator.

1585
01:27:26,860 --> 01:27:28,610
to live here in the first place

1586
01:27:28,700 --> 01:27:31,820
crummy old town?

1587
01:27:32,620 --> 01:27:35,200
-Wrong! Everything's wrong.

1588
01:27:35,290 --> 01:27:38,580
Why do we have to have all these kids?

1589
01:27:38,670 --> 01:27:42,330
-I don't know. Ask your mother.

1590
01:27:42,420 --> 01:27:44,170
-I'm going up to see Zuzu.

1591
01:27:44,250 --> 01:27:46,670
He told me to write a play for tomorrow.

1592
01:27:57,520 --> 01:28:01,270
F-r-a-n-k-i-n...

1593
01:28:01,480 --> 01:28:02,850
Hi, Daddy!

1594
01:28:03,980 --> 01:28:07,190
-I won a flower.

1595
01:28:07,490 --> 01:28:09,320
Where do you think you're going?

1596
01:28:09,400 --> 01:28:11,070
I want to give my flower a drink.

1597
01:28:11,160 --> 01:28:13,370
Now, give Daddy the flower.

1598
01:28:13,450 --> 01:28:14,780
I'll give it a drink.

1599
01:28:14,870 --> 01:28:16,200
Now, here.

1600
01:28:17,700 --> 01:28:19,790
Look, Daddy!

1601
01:28:19,870 --> 01:28:21,290
Paste it!

1602
01:28:21,370 --> 01:28:23,920
Yeah, all right, all right. Give it here.

1603
01:28:26,380 --> 01:28:28,920
Now, we'll paste this together here.

1604
01:28:32,140 --> 01:28:35,300
There. There it is. Good as new.

1605
01:28:35,390 --> 01:28:37,470
Now, give the flower a drink.

1606
01:28:37,560 --> 01:28:39,020
Now, will you do something for me?

1607
01:28:39,100 --> 01:28:41,850
-Will you try to get some sleep?

1608
01:28:42,060 --> 01:28:44,980
I want to look at my flower.

1609
01:28:45,060 --> 01:28:49,480
and then you can dream about it,

1610
01:28:49,780 --> 01:28:51,950
and it'll be a whole garden.

1611
01:28:52,030 --> 01:28:53,280
It will?

1612
01:29:01,710 --> 01:29:03,500
-Telephone!

1613
01:29:03,580 --> 01:29:05,000
I'll get it.

1614
01:29:06,920 --> 01:29:08,090
Hello?

1615
01:29:09,010 --> 01:29:11,050
Yes, this is Mrs. Bailey.

1616
01:29:11,420 --> 01:29:14,300
I'm sure she'll be all right.

1617
01:29:14,390 --> 01:29:16,010
that she ought to be out of bed

1618
01:29:16,100 --> 01:29:17,300
in time to have her Christmas dinner.

1619
01:29:17,390 --> 01:29:18,930
-Yes.

1620
01:29:19,020 --> 01:29:20,350
Let me speak to her.

1621
01:29:20,430 --> 01:29:22,890
Hello. Hello, Mrs. Welch?

1622
01:29:23,190 --> 01:29:25,730
This is George Bailey. I'm Zuzu's father.

1623
01:29:25,810 --> 01:29:27,520
are you, anyway?

1624
01:29:27,610 --> 01:29:29,900
sending her home like that, half naked?

1625
01:29:29,980 --> 01:29:32,530
with pneumonia on account of you?

1626
01:29:32,610 --> 01:29:34,570
-Is this the sort of thing we pay taxes for

1627
01:29:34,660 --> 01:29:36,780
to have teachers like you?

1628
01:29:36,870 --> 01:29:40,120
our kids home without any clothes on?

1629
01:29:40,200 --> 01:29:42,040
aren't the best-dressed kids.

1630
01:29:42,120 --> 01:29:43,870
any decent clothes...

1631
01:29:43,960 --> 01:29:45,750
That stupid...

1632
01:29:46,460 --> 01:29:49,380
Hello, Mrs. Welch. I want to apologize...

1633
01:29:49,460 --> 01:29:51,590
Hello? Hello.

1634
01:29:53,340 --> 01:29:55,760
-I'll hang her up!

1635
01:29:55,840 --> 01:29:59,050
-What is that?

1636
01:29:59,140 --> 01:30:00,930
Hello! Who's this?

1637
01:30:01,020 --> 01:30:02,560
Oh, Mr. Welch?

1638
01:30:02,930 --> 01:30:04,390
Okay, that's fine, Mr. Welch.

1639
01:30:04,480 --> 01:30:06,560
what I really think of your wife.

1640
01:30:06,650 --> 01:30:07,690
George, stop it.

1641
01:30:07,770 --> 01:30:09,480
Will you get out and let me handle this?

1642
01:30:09,570 --> 01:30:12,110
Hello? Hello? What?

1643
01:30:13,820 --> 01:30:15,400
Oh, you will, huh?

1644
01:30:15,490 --> 01:30:18,410
you think you're man enough, you...

1645
01:30:18,490 --> 01:30:19,990
Hello! Any...

1646
01:30:24,160 --> 01:30:25,120
Dad, how do you spell "hallelujah"?

1647
01:30:25,210 --> 01:30:27,250
What do you think I am, a dictionary?

1648
01:30:27,330 --> 01:30:28,580
Tommy, stop that! Stop it!

1649
01:30:28,670 --> 01:30:30,540
that silly tune yet?

1650
01:30:30,630 --> 01:30:34,340
Now stop it! Stop it!

1651
01:31:01,450 --> 01:31:03,080
I'm sorry, Mary.

1652
01:31:06,370 --> 01:31:08,250
Janie, I'm sorry.

1653
01:31:08,920 --> 01:31:13,090
You go on and practice.

1654
01:31:18,630 --> 01:31:21,010
Pete, I owe you an apology, too.

1655
01:31:22,260 --> 01:31:23,640
I'm sorry.

1656
01:31:25,060 --> 01:31:27,890
-Nothing, Daddy.

1657
01:31:34,860 --> 01:31:36,650
What's the matter with everybody?

1658
01:31:36,740 --> 01:31:39,280
Now, go on, play!

1659
01:31:39,360 --> 01:31:40,700
Oh, Daddy!

1660
01:31:46,080 --> 01:31:49,540
torture the children? Why don't you...

1661
01:31:50,290 --> 01:31:51,540
Mary...

1662
01:32:05,600 --> 01:32:07,520
Bedford 247, please.

1663
